<title>CANADA: CRICKET-INDIA 191 DEFEAT PAKSTAN 136.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-INDIA 191 DEFEAT PAKSTAN 136.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>India defeated Pakistan by 55</p>
<p>runs in the third match of the Sahara Cup cricket series at</p>
<p>the Toronto Cricket, Skating and Curling Club on Wednesday.</p>
<p>India were dismissed for 191, losing the last wicket on</p>
<p>the final ball of their 50 overs while Pakistan replied with</p>
<p>136 all out off 42.3 overs.</p>
<p>Scores:</p>
<p>India 191 (Rahul Dravid 46, Mohammad Azharuddin 38; Wasim</p>
<p>Akram four for 35)</p>
<p>Pakistan 136 (Moin Khan 42; Anil Kumble four for 12,</p>
<p>Venkatesh Prasad three for 22)</p>
<p>India leads the five-match series 2-1.</p>
<p>The final two matches will be played on Saturday and</p>
<p>Sunday.</p>
</text>
